{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification"],"declarations":23,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.partitionDom_not_iff_lexGt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.partitionDom_not_iff_lexGt","kind":"theorem","line":305,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionLex.lean#L305-L308","doc":"The dominance bridge is therefore **strictly** one-directional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.lexGt_nu411_lam33_via_colLen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.lexGt_nu411_lam33_via_colLen","kind":"theorem","line":294,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionLex.lean#L294-L303","doc":"**Non-vacuity: the column criterion derives the separating instance.**\n\nSame conclusion as `dom_fails_lex_holds.1`, obtained through `lexGt_of_colLen`\ninstead of by exhibiting the witness by hand.  So the engine fires on the shape of\nstep the Garnir relation produces, rather than being a criterion nothing satisfies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.colLen_nu411_of_three_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.colLen_nu411_of_three_lt","kind":"theorem","line":286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionLex.lean#L286-L292","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.colLen_nu411_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.colLen_nu411_three","kind":"theorem","line":274,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionLex.lean#L274-L284","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.colLen_lam33_of_three_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.colLen_lam33_of_three_lt","kind":"theorem","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionLex.lean#L271-L272","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.colLen_lam33_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.colLen_lam33_three","kind":"theorem","line":263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionLex.lean#L263-L269","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.dom_fails_lex_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.dom_fails_lex_holds","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionLex.lean#L231-L249","doc":"**The separating example: lex holds where dominance fails.**\n\n`(4,1,1) >ₗ (3,3)` because `4 > 3` in the first row, but `(4,1,1)` does *not*\ndominate `(3,3)` because `4 + 1 = 5 < 6 = 3 + 3`.\n\nThis is exactly the pair Mathas' Garnir composition produces at `λ = (3,3)`, node\n`(0,1)`, so the failure is not a curiosity about the two orders — it is the\ninduction step of Lemma 3.12 refusing to be a dominance step.\n\nOnly rows `0` and `1` are ever inspected: the lex witness is row `0`, and dominance\nalready fails at the partial sum over `{0, 1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.rowLen_nu411_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.rowLen_nu411_one","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionLex.lean#L228-L229","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.rowLen_nu411_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.rowLen_nu411_zero","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionLex.lean#L225-L226","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.rowLen_lam33_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.rowLen_lam33_one","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionLex.lean#L222-L223","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.rowLen_lam33_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.rowLen_lam33_zero","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionLex.lean#L219-L220","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.nu411","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.nu411","kind":"def","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionLex.lean#L215-L217","doc":"`(4,1,1)`, the partition of Mathas' Garnir composition at `λ = (3,3)`, node\n`(i,j) = (0,1)`: the composition is `(1, 4, 1)`, which sorts to this. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.lam33","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.lam33","kind":"def","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionLex.lean#L212-L213","doc":"`(3,3)`, the shape of the counterexample. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.lexGt_of_colLen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.lexGt_of_colLen","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionLex.lean#L165-L203","doc":"**The column-length criterion for a lex step.**\n\nIf `ν` has strictly more parts exceeding `k` than `μ` does, and exactly as many\nparts exceeding every larger threshold, then `ν >ₗ μ` — with the witness named:\n`μ.colLen k`, the number of parts of `μ` above `k`.\n\nThis is the shape of every Garnir step.  Naming the witness rather than leaving it\nexistential is what the probe measured: it is **not** the Garnir row `i`.  At\n`λ = (2,2,2)` with node `(i,j) = (1,0)` the new shape is `(3,2,1)`, which first\ndiffers from `λ` at row `0`, because the merged part overtakes the rows above `i`\nthat tie with `λᵢ`.  `μ.colLen k` gets that right; `i` does not.\n\nThe proof needs no sorting.  Below the witness both diagrams contain every column\n`j ≤ k` (their column lengths there are at least `μ.colLen k`, which exceeds the row\nindex) and agree above `k` by hypothesis, so the rows match.  At the witness the\nhypothesis at `k` separates them: `ν` still has column `k`, `μ` does not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.rowLen_eq_of_colLen_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.rowLen_eq_of_colLen_iff","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionLex.lean#L157-L163","doc":"Row length is pinned by the column lengths, threshold by threshold. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.eq_of_lt_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.eq_of_lt_iff","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionLex.lean#L150-L155","doc":"Two naturals with the same strict lower sets are equal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.lexGt_of_partitionDom_of_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.lexGt_of_partitionDom_of_ne","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionLex.lean#L102-L128","doc":"**Mathas' note: dominance implies lex.**  \"Note that if `λ ⊵ μ` then `λ > μ`.\"\n\nThis is the bridge that keeps the corpus's existing dominance results usable: every\n`partitionDom` fact still yields a lex fact, so switching the Garnir induction to lex\ncosts nothing already proved.  The converse is false — see `dom_fails_lex_holds`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.partitionLexGt_trans","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.partitionLexGt_trans","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionLex.lean#L84-L100","doc":"Lex is transitive.  The witness is the smaller of the two indices; the three\ncases differ only in which side supplies the strict step. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.ne_of_partitionLexGt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.ne_of_partitionLexGt","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionLex.lean#L79-L82","doc":"A lex-greater shape is a different shape. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.partitionLexGt_irrefl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.partitionLexGt_irrefl","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionLex.lean#L74-L77","doc":"Lex is irreflexive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.eq_of_rowLen_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.eq_of_rowLen_eq","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionLex.lean#L64-L72","doc":"Equal row lengths at every index means equal diagrams.\n\nThe same `mem_iff_lt_rowLen` step `partitionDom_antisymm` runs on, factored out\nbecause both the irreflexivity and the dominance bridge below need it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.«term_>ₗ_»","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.«term_>ₗ_»","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionLex.lean#L62-L62","doc":"**Lexicographic order on Young diagrams**: `μ >_lex ν` iff the first row length\nat which they differ is larger in `μ`.\n\nStated with the witnessing index explicit, matching Mathas' phrasing (\"there exists\nan integer `j`\"), and indexed from `0` rather than his `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.partitionLexGt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionLex.partitionLexGt","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PartitionLex.lean#L54-L60","doc":"**Lexicographic order on Young diagrams**: `μ >_lex ν` iff the first row length\nat which they differ is larger in `μ`.\n\nStated with the witnessing index explicit, matching Mathas' phrasing (\"there exists\nan integer `j`\"), and indexed from `0` rather than his `1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}